# Stakeholder mail

Copyright (c) 2026 Devrecated.

Send Autodevelop-hosted mail only after an explicit yes.

- Show **to, subject, HTML-as-text, ticket link, host origin** and wait.
- Recipients must be on the instance `mail.allowlist` or the org member list. To send elsewhere, the user must retype the address or the override phrase.
- Run `send-stakeholder-mail.mjs` with `--confirm <token>`. No token → do not send.
- The script posts `POST /cli/mail`. It does not write Firestore `mail` unless `mail.transport` is `firestore`.
- Hooks never send mail, never write `mail`, and never invent a confirm token.
- Do not use Mail.app, mailto, or a Gmail API.
- Do not log the message body, tokens, or raw PII.
- Firestore transport must not target a project in `forbiddenProjects`.
